0..74 Comment "// Calls nested inside a path type\'s endpoints convert to their values. An"
75..150 Comment "// endpoint that applies a function to another call waits on the inner call"
151..227 Comment "// once the outer one unfolds, and conversion unfolds that call next; over a"
228..302 Comment "// presented type the inner call stands under a constructor the outer call"
303..380 Comment "// built, and the normal form reads it before the rules run. An endpoint that"
381..455 Comment "// applies the function a call returns is the bind over that call applying"
456..524 Comment "// what it binds. Conversion is definitional equality by computation"
525..591 Comment "// (Martin-Löf, _Intuitionistic Type Theory_, Bibliopolis, 1984)."
593..670 Comment "// The free naturals, the presented integers and their steps `up` and `down`."
